# Config-change hook: core runs every script in rc.syshook.d/config/ after a
# config save (Config::save -> syslog config-event -> configd
# system.event.config_changed -> rc.syshook config). Queue a reconcile of the
# managed tunnels' IPv6 addresses and routes, the default-route guard and the
# rendered rules, and return at once: core runs these hooks one after another
# and skips config events while they run. The reconcile is idempotent and
# silent unless it repairs something, so the plugin's own saves do not loop.
# It never writes config.

/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/OPNsense/WGClientTunnels/wgct.sh request_reconcile
exit 0
